ns.xlsx","locator":"Operating 4471!A8:E23 and Payroll 6158!A8:E26; balance per bank, outstanding payments, balance per books, unrecorded charges and preparer","sha256":"f27ecd2650767fffdb5de9c366f4e409f73c8438e38a9e578f38c63bfce48415","name":"E04 Payroll 6158","originalSheet":"Payroll 6158","kind":"rec","primary":false},{"source":"02 Confirmations/Bank confirmation request.pdf","locator":"PDF page 1; the accounts, the balances per the customer, the questions asked and the customer’s authorization","sha256":"3d69ab318029200dba39c605613d1832c5504e7a5bc1f12f2ecc46d21d0e6f73","name":"E05 Request","originalSheet":null,"kind":"request","primary":true},{"source":"02 Confirmations/Cinderbrook Bank confirmation.pdf","locator":"PDF page 1; the balance of each deposit account and loan, the accrued interest and the signature","sha256":"e19af9bbed5303b885a9fdf5e8321f9b61a3636a37327a5a2e943657f05e3538","name":"E06 Confirmation","originalSheet":null,"kind":"bank","primary":true},{"source":"02 Confirmations/Cinderbrook Bank supplementary reply.pdf","locator":"PDF page 1; service charges, check 21561, stale checks, holds, liens, set-off and compensating balances","sha256":"d82635408c8a91d4073a579433122797e0b3632d2a3cd3f8e2744c348eb2f3a9","name":"E07 Supplementary Reply","originalSheet":null,"kind":"detail","primary":true},{"source":"03 Bank Statements/June 2026 bank statements.pdf","locator":"PDF pages 1-4; the June 2026 statements of both accounts, every line and the closing balances","sha256":"d06925c33977aa3f9b70d3f4f4ad789fcabdc131ca8277e6f6f5e2fd06e4ae7b","name":"E09 June Statements","originalSheet":null,"kind":"june","primary":true},{"source":"03 Bank Statements/July 1 to 8 2026 cutoff statement.pdf","locator":"PDF pages 1-2; the July 1 to 8, 2026 cutoff statement of both accounts, sent by the bank directly","sha256":"f0c3ee45832fe941da797c5a0195388569965a7d00a4bec3eadae2c571d7bb24","name":"E10 Cutoff Statement","originalSheet":null,"kind":"july","primary":true},{"source":"02 Confirmations/Cinderbrook Bank incoming payments report.xlsx","locator":"Incoming Payments!A8:F14; every credit to the operating account June 15 to July 8, 2026, received and credited","sha256":"0ef0ade1fb545a41b4a8c4ce37d1701447c4d10c29a19f64945ae092d84cbc3a","name":"E08 Incoming Payments","originalSheet":"Incoming Payments","kind":"receipts","primary":true}],"openItems":[{"id":"FEE-01","status":"open","amount":"4065.00","explanation":"The bank’s 12 monthly charges on the payroll account ending 6158, $4,065.00 for FY2026, were never recorded. Payroll cash is overstated and expenses understated by $4,065.00. Proposed adjustment: debit a bank charges expense, credit 1020 payroll cash. It is under the $17,000.00 clearly trivial, so it is listed and not added up; the CPA may pass it. The bank feed should post the charges each month. The machine never posts."},{"id":"STALE-01","status":"open","amount":"21850.80","explanation":"Check 21561, $21,850.80, to Sound Waste & Recycling Co. for invoice SWR-2511-1294 of December 18, 2025, has never been presented and was 194 days old at June 30, past the bank’s 180-day limit. The vendor has not been paid, yet the books count the invoice as paid. Ask the Controller to contact the vendor and reissue it or void it with a stop payment. If voided: debit 1010 operating cash, credit 2000 accounts payable (or an unclaimed property liability). Above clearly trivial; a classification with no effect on income."},{"id":"CONF-01","status":"open","amount":"188441.43","explanation":"The bank confirmed $5,723,107.14; the request showed the books’ $5,534,665.71. The $188,441.43 difference is explained in full: 8 checks that cleared July 1 to 7 ($170,655.63), plus check 21561 ($21,850.80), less the payroll account charges ($4,065.00). No adjustment beyond FEE-01 and STALE-01. The CPA accepts the explanation or asks for more."},{"id":"REC-01","status":"open","amount":null,"explanation":"Both June 30 reconciliations were prepared by Marisol Zielinski, Project Accountant, on July 12, 2026 and foot, but neither is signed as reviewed: the control walkthroughs’ REC-01 (CLS-2). The charges sat on the payroll reconciliation all year and the December check went unfollowed. Recommendation: the Controller signs each reconciliation within 15 days and follows up any item older than 60 days."},{"id":"DISC-01","status":"open","amount":"5473107.14","explanation":"All of the company’s cash, $5,723,107.14 per the bank, is at one bank, Cinderbrook Bank; $5,473,107.14 is above the FDIC’s $250,000.00 insurance. The draft notes have no concentration of credit risk note. Disclosure is a judgment for the CPA. No cash is restricted, pledged or held back, and the loans require no compensating balance."},{"id":"XREF-01","status":"open","amount":"28665.00","explanation":"The bank confirms interest accrued June 1 to 30, 2026 of $17,040.00 (term loan ending 2208) and $11,625.00 (line ending 3315), paid through May 31 and debited July 1. The books record interest when debited: the liabilities search’s UL-04 and the covenant procedures’ INT-01. Not counted again here."},{"id":"MAT-01","status":"open","amount":"340000.00","explanation":"Materiality is proposed at $340,000.00, 0.5% of revenue; performance materiality $255,000.00; clearly trivial $17,000.00. The engagement partner sets it."},{"id":"SIGN-01","status":"open","amount":null,"explanation":"These are draft workpapers and a draft findings memo for the engagement partner. They are not an audit report and give no opinion. Nothing has been posted, signed or sent to the client or the bank."}],"incomplete":true,"research":null,"filing":"audit-cash-hgc","returnFile":"Audit Findings DRAFT.pdf","returnLabel":"Draft Findings Memo for the CPA","periodLabel":"Fiscal year ended June 30, 2026"}